# Understand Anything incremental in {{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/

Before any action with Understand Anything in this repo, read `AGENTS.md` and
the architecture document that governs this mechanism, when present.

## Blocking rule

The graph uses `PROJECT_ROOT={{ harness_understand_apps_root }}`, while Git uses
the repository root. Incremental changed files must therefore be relative to
`{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/`.

Use:

```bash
bash .harness/lib/understand-apps-changed-files.sh
```

or:

```bash
LAST=$(node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const m=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json','utf8')); process.stdout.write(m.gitCommitHash)")
git diff --relative={{ harness_understand_apps_root }} "$LAST"..HEAD --name-only -- {{ harness_understand_apps_root }} | rg -v '^\.understand-anything/'
```

Never hardcode the graph hash; read `gitCommitHash` from the provider metadata.

## Forbidden

```bash
git diff <lastCommitHash>..HEAD --name-only
git -C {{ harness_understand_apps_root }} diff <lastCommitHash>..HEAD --name-only
```

Those commands emit paths with the project-root prefix, but the provider expects
paths relative to its own root.

## Checklist

1. Confirm `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json` exists.
2. Generate changed files with the canonical helper.
3. Reject entries prefixed with `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/` or rooted in docs/tooling.
4. Run incremental without `--full`.
5. Validate the provider graph through the repository Knowledge Graph contract.
